  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Structuring the Folders**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing a modular folder structure for the backend and frontend. The example outlines a `/`, `.env.example`, `server.ts` for the backend entry point with Vite middleware, and `src/` for the React frontend, including `main.tsx` and `App.tsx`. I believe this will provide an excellent basis.\n\n\n**Defining the Frontend Structure**\n\nI\'m now structuring the frontend components. I\'m leaning towards a `/page_shell` directory. Inside, I plan to include shared types, services (Gemini API client, prompt builder), routes (API handlers), and components (Navbar, HeroSection, ResumeInput, JobDescriptionInput, OptimizeButton, ResultCard). This design emphasizes a clear separation of concerns.\n\n\n**Integrating Gemini API**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Gemini API for text tasks, specifically ATS resume analysis and rewriting. I\'m using the `@google/genai` SDK and initializing the API with the `gemini-3.6-flash` model. I\'ve defined a request structure that includes resume and job description inputs, with validation checks for non-empty strings and length limits. I\'m focusing on getting structured JSON responses, either directly from Gemini using a defined schema or by parsing a clean JSON output.\n\n\n**Defining the Response Schema**\n\nI\'m solidifying the response schema now. I plan on including `matchScore` (percentage match), `keyKeywordsMatched`, `missingKeywordsAdded`, `strengthsSummary`, the `optimizedResume` as markdown, and `formattingTips` for ATS submission. The JSON format should be easy for the frontend to digest. I feel I am ready to implement the analysis now.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Engineering the Prompts**\n\nI\'m focused on the prompt engineering now. I need the output to adhere strictly to the schema. I\'m taking the user requirements of analysis, keyword extraction, and accurate rewrites, and translating these into specific instructions for the model. I\'ll need to stress factual accuracy and avoid fabricated content in the prompts. I want to build a resume rewriting workflow.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 601662595
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
