    replacement_chunks {
      replacement_content: "import { SampleData } from \'../types.js\';\n\nexport const SAMPLE_DATASETS: SampleData[] = [\n  {\n    title: \'Senior Software Engineer\',\n    role: \'Full-Stack Developer\',\n    resume: `Alex Rivera\nSoftware Developer | alex.rivera@email.com | (555) 234-5678 | San Francisco, CA\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\nDeveloper with 3+ years experience building web applications. Good knowledge of JavaScript, React, HTML, CSS, and basic Node.js. Passionate about learning new technologies and writing clean code.\n\nEXPERIENCE\nSoftware Developer at Acme Web Corp (2022 - Present)\n- Built web pages using React and Tailwind CSS.\n- Fixed bugs and improved app loading times.\n- Worked with backend team on API integrations.\n- Created UI components and wrote unit tests.\n\nJunior Developer at TechStart Inc. (2021 - 2022)\n- Maintained client websites and updated content.\n- Assisted with database queries and HTML updates.\n- Attended daily standups and sprint planning.\n\nSKILLS\nJavaScript, React, HTML, CSS, Git, Node.js, SQL, REST APIs\n\nEDUCATION\nB.S. in Computer Science - University of California (2021)`,\n    jobDescription: `Senior Full Stack Engineer (React / Node.js / TypeScript)\n\nWe are seeking a Senior Full Stack Engineer to lead the architecture and development of our high-scale cloud platform.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n- Design, build, and deploy resilient microservices using Node.js, Express, and TypeScript.\n- Craft performant, accessible user interfaces using React 19, Next.js/Vite, and Tailwind CSS.\n- Optimize REST and GraphQL APIs for maximum latency and throughput.\n- Implement CI/CD pipelines, Docker containers, and cloud deployment on AWS/GCP.\n- Drive automated testing (Jest, Cypress), code reviews, and technical documentation.\n\nRequirements:\n- 5+ years of full-stack engineering experience.\n- Deep expertise in TypeScript, React, Node.js, System Architecture, and SQL/NoSQL databases.\n- Strong background in performance optimization, state management, and security best practices.`,\n  },\n  {\n    title: \'Product Manager\',\n    role: \'Product & Strategy\',\n    resume: `Jordan Hayes\nAssociate Product Specialist | jordan.hayes@email.com | Chicago, IL\n\nSUMMARY\nProduct professional with 2 years of experience supporting software releases, gathering user feedback, and writing user stories. Strong communication skills.\n\nEXPERIENCE\nProduct Specialist at SaaSify (2023 - Present)\n- Gathered requirements from customer success and sales teams.\n- Created tickets in Jira and tracked team progress.\n- Conducted user interviews to identify pain points.\n- Prepared monthly release notes for stakeholders.\n\nProject Coordinator at Digital Media Group (2022 - 2023)\n- Managed project schedules and team deadlines.\n- Organized meetings and documented decisions.\n\nSKILLS\nJira, Confluence, User Research, Agile, Communication, Roadmapping basics, Excel`,\n    jobDescription: `Senior Technical Product Manager - AI & Cloud Platform\n\nWe are hiring a Senior Product Manager to own our core AI product roadmap from discovery to execution.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n- Define product vision, strategy, and OKRs for our flagship AI platform.\n- Translate complex customer needs into clear PRDs, user stories, and acceptance criteria.\n- Partner closely with AI research engineers, UI/UX designers, and go-to-market teams.\n- Conduct quantitative cohort analysis, funnel tracking (Mixpanel/Amplitude), and A/B testing.\n- Prioritize product backlogs using data-driven frameworks (RICE, Kano).\n\nRequirements:\n- 4+ years of B2B SaaS Product Management experience.\n- Demonstrated success launching AI or data-intensive software products.\n- Mastery of Agile/Scrum, product analytics tools, SQL, wireframing, and stakeholder alignment.`,\n  },\n  {\n    title: \'Data Analyst / Scientist\',\n    role: \'Data & Analytics\',\n    resume: `Morgan Chen\nData Analyst | m.chen@email.com | New York, NY\n\nSUMMARY\nAnalytical thinker with 2 years experience working with SQL databases and Excel. Created basic dashboards in Tableau and generated weekly reports for sales teams.\n\nEXPERIENCE\nJunior Data Analyst at Retail Insights (2023 - Present)\n- Pulled data from MySQL database using SQL queries.\n- Maintained weekly sales report spreadsheets in Excel.\n- Built 3 Tableau dashboards for executive leadership.\n- Cleaned raw data using Python scripts.\n\nSKILLS\nSQL, Excel, Python (Pandas), Tableau, Data Cleaning, Basic Statistics\n\nEDUCATION\nB.A. in Economics - New York University (2022)`,\n    jobDescription: `Lead Data Scientist & Analytics Engineer\n\nLooking for an experienced Data Scientist to transform massive behavioral datasets into strategic actionable insights and automated ML predictive models.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n- Build statistical models, machine learning algorithms, and predictive forecasting pipelines.\n- Write complex ETL/ELT pipelines using Snowflake, dbt, Python (PySpark/Pandas), and BigQuery.\n- Design interactive executive dashboards in PowerBI/Tableau with automated data refreshing.\n- Perform hypothesis testing, cohort retention modeling, and customer lifetime value (LTV) attribution.\n\nRequirements:\n- Master\'s or Bachelor\'s in Quantitative Field (Statistics, CS, Economics).\n- 4+ years experience in Data Science or Analytics Engineering.\n- Deep proficiency in Advanced SQL, Python (Scikit-Learn, Pandas, NumPy), A/B Testing, and Cloud Data Warehouses.`,\n  },\n];\n"
    }
